FINAL CHECK

Before emitting JSON, verify exact rank and context-ID coverage, then audit
every term for disjoint common concrete, verbal or grammatical, and abstract
or institutional senses that genuinely apply in the selected period. Do not
repeat or paraphrase the contextual sense as an additional sense.

Treat every ranked spelling as one complete lexical item: never define,
pronounce, or exemplify only a component character, substring, or stem. Every
generated sentence must use that complete item naturally, in the exact
supplied spelling where grammar permits or in one ordinary inflected form
where grammar requires it. Do not use a different derivative or longer
compound, and include no HTML or formatting. Every aligned translation must be
natural English translating the complete source sentence.

Cross-check each contextual translation, definition, part of speech, nuance,
and pronunciation against the marked occurrence in the full passage. For a
polyphonic spelling, select the reading belonging to that exact contextual
sense; for a multi-part term, preserve the contribution of the whole term.
Reject any generated example whose grammar or translation demonstrates a
different listed sense.

Keep every dictionary meaning conservative: explain one coherent lexical
sense of the complete term without translating the whole passage, conflating
senses, or asserting unsupported arguments, etymology, cultural facts, or
interpretive claims. For historical language, do not import a later cognate or
rare, out-of-period use as though it were ordinary. Verify that every complete
passage translation is faithful, complete, natural English and adds no
substantive participant, circumstance, modality, or claim absent from the
source.
